  "intro": "Albuquerque is the best-sited city for radio in the country, and the reason is Sandia Crest. A 10,600-foot ridge sits directly above the eastern suburbs with a road to the top, and effectively every repeater in central New Mexico lives on it. From up there a five-watt handheld covers an area the size of a small country. Down in the valley, Kirtland puts military traffic on the UHF airband and the Rio Grande corridor carries the freight line east to west.",
  "introz": "阿尔伯克基是全美对无线电最友好的城市，原因就是桑迪亚峰。一道三千二百米的山脊直接压在东郊上方，有公路直达峰顶，新墨西哥州中部几乎所有中继都设在那里。在峰顶，一台五瓦手台覆盖的面积相当于一个小国家。山下的河谷里，柯特兰基地把军航通话送上 UHF 波段，格兰德河走廊则承载着东西向的货运干线。",
